# Fear, sadness, surprise, amusement, attraction, embarrassment, disgust: the rest of the range, then back to business.
# speaker | what the customer does (their goal, in their own words) | what Mara faces
elf | Lean in and warn her quietly that the men who burned the mill last week were asking about her stall. | The elf quietly warns her that the men who burned the mill were asking about her stall.
warrior | Tell her not to worry, you will stand by the stall a while. | The warrior offers to stand guard by her stall.
elf | Tell her gently that the orchard beyond town was among the farms that burned. | The elf tells her the orchard she buys from has burned.
warrior | Try to cheer her up with a terrible joke about a pear. | The warrior tells her a terrible joke about a pear to cheer her up.
warrior | Compliment her eyes and ask, with a grin, if she is free after market. | The warrior flirts, praising her eyes and asking if she is free after market.
elf | Point out, with a straight face, that a rat is nibbling the plums behind her. | The elf points out a rat nibbling her plums.
elf | Tell her a caravan master is coming tomorrow wanting two hundred apples, and you will send him to her. | The elf tells her a caravan master wants two hundred apples tomorrow and will be sent to her.
warrior | Ask what she needs most right now. | The warrior asks what she needs most right now.
